Build-time only patch, applied inside the container to the copied sources.

The 1C mobile platform loads an external component on Android differently from
the desktop platform, and the component has to be built for that platform
without touching the shared sources of the project.

1. Android ships no cyrus-sasl, so the SASL2 block of the main CMakeLists.txt
   is skipped there. SASL needs no external library: librdkafka implements
   SCRAM on its own, and OAUTHBEARER comes with the TLS runtime of vcpkg.

2. The ABI of the build is reported in the log of the container build.

The entry point JNI_OnLoad, which the mobile platform requires, is not part of
this patch: src/jnienv.cpp is compiled into the library for Android by the
main CMakeLists.txt, and the symbol is exported through src/version.script.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -208,7 +208,8 @@
 # -----------------------------
 # Linux SASL2 (if librdkafka is built with SASL support)
 # -----------------------------
-if (UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+# Android ships no cyrus-sasl, so it is neither found nor linked there.
+if (UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT ANDROID)
     find_package(PkgConfig REQUIRED)
     pkg_check_modules(SASL2 REQUIRED libsasl2)
     target_include_directories(${TARGET} PRIVATE ${SASL2_INCLUDE_DIRS})
@@ -220,3 +221,7 @@
 # -----------------------------
 message(STATUS "CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE: ${CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE}")
 message(STATUS "VCPKG_TARGET_TRIPLET: ${VCPKG_TARGET_TRIPLET}")
+if (ANDROID)
+    message(STATUS "ANDROID_ABI: ${ANDROID_ABI}")
+    message(STATUS "ANDROID_PLATFORM: ${ANDROID_PLATFORM}")
+endif()
